WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.040
My family moved here through the Ledouxs, and the Mosses and Vincents.

2
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.480
On my other side of my family is the Vincents.

3
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:18.940
So I guess more or less I am related on two aspects of the original descendants of Mossville.

4
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.440
Who were the original descendants of Mossville?

5
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:30.640
As far as I know, it was the Mosses, the Braxtons, the Rigmaidens, Vincents, and the Ledouxs.

6
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:34.860
According to Dad, my great-grandmother was a Ledoux,

7
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:43.740
and apparently she owned some property in that two hundred acres that Sasol has negotiated to buy forty some acres from,

8
00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.720
I was told she has nine plots of land in there.

9
00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:49.420
So when you moved to Mossville, you were eight years old.

10
00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:51.820
What is the earliest memory you have of Mossville?

11
00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.300
Like what was that earliest memory you have of it?

12
00:00:54.300 --> 00:01:02.060
Playing up and down Old Spanish Trail when it was about maybe six and a half, seven foot wide.

13
00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:09.800
Only one car could go down on the hard surface at a time and when you met someone from the opposite direction,

14
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:13.960
you had one set of tires on, and one set of tires in the gravel.

15
00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:17.060
[laughs] So how did Mossville look at that time?

16
00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:21.400
Very green, quiet, neighborly.

17
00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:25.180
You could play in other neighbors’ yards and there was no problem.

18
00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:32.440
If you got into trouble in that neighbor's yard you got a spanking there and when you got home you found out there was one waiting for you there also.

19
00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:36.920
So Prater Road is named after your grandfather.

20
00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:40.580
Was that road already named after him when you guys moved here?

21
00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:41.160
Yes.

22
00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:45.060
That road at one time was nothing but a dirt road.

23
00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:49.960
And every time we would have a hard, hard rain it would flood.

24
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:57.040
So a group of kids would always get out into the middle of the street with their shoes off and go wading, playing in the water.

25
00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:02.260
My father's family went to Mount Zion, which is the oldest church in this area.

26
00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:07.740
And my family went to a church that was a branch of Mount Zion, which is Willow Springs.

27
00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:12.140
Mount Zion is 140 plus years, and Willow Springs is one 105 years old.
